    Adds docs/traceability-doctrine.md: the contract every board row, commit
    trailer and test-provenance comment in this repository is read against, plus a
    one-section pointer in README.md (### Traceability).
    
    The contract states that a marker is one physical line,
    `ch:trace row=<id> key=value ...`, whose every field is either a value a reader
    can resolve or an explicit `none:<reason>`; silence is not an answer, and a
    missing key is weaker than any `none:`. It defines the nine core fields -
    row, spec, wave, test, evidence, witness, verdict, commit, memory - with the
    concrete forms observed in this repo, the verification command for each, and
    what a reader may conclude from a `none:`. Two extension keys (doc, prompt) are
    documented as additions, never replacements.
    
    `witness` is defined honestly as the anti-tautology field: evidence is what the
